NOTICE — provenance of internal/kb/testdata

This directory holds the fixed corpus used by the golden retrieval tests in
internal/kb. Nothing here is shipped in the Conduit binary; it exists only so
that retrieval behaviour can be pinned byte-for-byte across the v2 rebuild.

corpus/ contents and provenance
--------------------------------

01-gettysburg-address.txt
    Excerpt: "The Gettysburg Address", Abraham Lincoln, 19 November 1863
    (Bliss copy). A work of the United States federal government, published
    long before 1929. PUBLIC DOMAIN worldwide.

02-declaration-preamble.txt
    Excerpt: preamble of the United States Declaration of Independence, 1776.
    A work of the United States federal government, published long before 1929.
    PUBLIC DOMAIN worldwide.

03-moby-dick-loomings.txt
    Excerpt: opening of Chapter 1 ("Loomings") of "Moby-Dick; or, The Whale",
    Herman Melville, 1851. Published before 1929; author died 1891.
    PUBLIC DOMAIN worldwide.

04-alice-down-the-rabbit-hole.txt
    Excerpt: opening of Chapter 1 ("Down the Rabbit-Hole") of "Alice's
    Adventures in Wonderland", Lewis Carroll (Charles Lutwidge Dodgson), 1865.
    Published before 1929; author died 1898. PUBLIC DOMAIN worldwide.

05-sonnet-18.txt
    "Sonnet 18" ("Shall I compare thee to a summer's day?"), William
    Shakespeare, first published 1609. PUBLIC DOMAIN worldwide.

06-fixture-lantern-keeper.txt
07-fixture-harbour-ledger.txt
    ORIGINAL WORK written for this repository by the Conduit maintainers and
    contributed under the repository's own licence (see /LICENSE). These two
    files are synthetic: they exist to give the tests a controlled term
    frequency gradient ("lantern") and a paragraph that appears verbatim in two
    different documents. They are not quotations of anyone else's text.

Notes on the excerpts
---------------------

The public-domain excerpts have been lightly normalised for test stability:
em dashes and typographic quotation marks were replaced with ASCII equivalents,
and long paragraphs were re-wrapped. The wording is otherwise unchanged. These
files are fixtures, not scholarly editions; do not cite them as such.

Total size of this directory is kept under 200 KB deliberately. Anything larger
belongs outside the repository.
